WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.940
SPEAKER 1: On August 5, 1857, a
4,300-kilometer-long cable was

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.600
laid across the Atlantic Ocean.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.650
It provided a link between
Britain and the Americas,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.470
further strengthening their
social and economic alliances.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.620
Now, information
could be represented

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.800
as a pattern of
electrical pulses

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.630
and sent across the world
almost instantaneously.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.830
Stock tickers and
money transfers,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.630
these were commercial
applications

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.830
invented by Western
Union which ushered

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.420
in a new era of
global communication.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.170
SPEAKER 2: Stand by
for this announcement.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.520
Germany has invaded Poland
and has bombed many towns.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.400
General mobilization has been
ordered in Britain and France.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.850
SPEAKER 3: And
consequently, this country

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.100
is at war with Germany.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.570
SPEAKER 4:
--throughout the world

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.664
which is the real
cause of the war,

00:00:59.664 --> 00:01:03.456
that today threatens
the freedom of mankind.

00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:10.570
SPEAKER 5:
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:16.904
SPEAKER 6:
[SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

00:01:16.904 --> 00:01:19.320
SPEAKER 7: The Japanese have
attacked Pearl Harbor, Hawaii

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.650
by air, President Roosevelt
has just announced.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.340
ADOLPH HITLER: [SPEAKING GERMAN]

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.970
SPEAKER 1: During World War
II, Germany, Italy, and Japan

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:30.240
were far outnumbered
by the Allies.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.830
Their only conceivable
path the victory

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:37.020
was the ability to launch
widespread surprise attacks.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.930
So the goal of
encryption technology

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:43.860
was to automate the one-time
pad using an encryption machine.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.820
Ideally, this machine would
accept an input letter,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.970
apply a random shift, and
output the encrypted letter.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.370
However, all machines
follow the same principle.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.300
They begin in some initial
configuration known as a state.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.460
They accept some input.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.830
They do an operation
with the input.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.670
And then they produce an output.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:11.050
The operation from initial
state to final state

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.750
is always predictable
and repeatable.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.580
So the goal was to produce
identical machines that

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.110
output a scrambled
sequence of shifts

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.155
which took a long
time to repeat.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.970
Therefore Alice and Bob could
generate an identical shift

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.470
sequence as follows.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.950
First, they need to
share identical machines

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.200
and agree on an
initial position, which

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.610
is defined as the key setting.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.076
Then, they align their
machines to the same position.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.840
And finally, cycle through
the identical operations

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.770
to achieve identical sequences.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.360
Now the state of the art
technology at the time

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.370
was called a rotor
encryption machine.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.930
We are all familiar with
the mechanical process

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.700
of an odometer which
takes a long time

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.860
to finally repeat its cycle.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.230
Now, imagine we
scrambled the numbers

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.650
on the wheels of the odometer.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.630
When it ticks
forward, a new shift

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.740
could be generated by adding
up each number on the rotors.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.020
This is the rough idea behind
rotor encryption machines.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.200
For example, the message
"attack northwest"

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.585
would be encrypted as follows.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.730
Notice how a new shift
is used at each position

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.100
in the message.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.500
With three rotors,
each with 26 numbers,

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.070
the length of this
sequence, before repeating,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.870
is 26 times 26 times 26.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.240
This is equivalent to
having a list of shifts

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.930
17,576 numbers long.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.770
Understand that
each rotor position

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.670
is equivalent to a
location in this sequence.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:07.090
The initial machine state
is known as the key setting.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:10.720
And the collection of
all possible key settings

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.960
defines the key space.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.100
This key space increases
if the number of ways

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.029
to initially configure
the machine increases.

00:04:20.029 --> 00:04:23.940
For example, if the
rotors can be rearranged,

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.560
then the order can be
selected in six ways.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.110
Let's visualize the key
space at this point.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:37.850
First, we choose from one of
six possible rotor orderings.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.140
Then we select an
initial position

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.275
from the rotor sequence.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:50.110
This gives us a key space with
over 100,000 key settings.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:53.100
Remember, every
machine configuration

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.860
is a point in this space.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:00.140
When we select a key setting, we
are selecting a starting point

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.820
in this space which
then determines

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.450
the rest of the shift sequence.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.050
Give away the key
setting, and you give away

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.900
the entire sequence.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.590
The security of rotor
machines depends

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:15.740
on both the size
of this key space

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.880
and the randomness
of the key setting.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.720
During World War II, one of
the most important encryption

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.780
technologies used by
the German military

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.900
was known as the Enigma.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.330
It was an electromechanical
rotor machine

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.990
invented by a German engineer
at the end of World War

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.320
I. Each rotor wheel
had electrical contacts

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:41.710
on either side with a
maze of wirings within.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.400
So at each rotor position,
there was an electrical path

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:49.080
from every input letter
to every output letter.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.600
When the rotor advanced,
an entirely new path

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.470
was defined for each letter.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.700
During the war, they
continually tried

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.400
to increase the key
space of the Enigma

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.800
in order to make it stronger.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.680
For example, some
changes they made

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.110
were to add a fourth
rotor wheel and increase

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:12.280
the number of possible rotors
you could put into the machine

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.480
to 60.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.860
This had the effect of massively
increasing the key space.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.550
Near the end of
the war, the Enigma

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:24.480
could be set up in over 150
million million million ways.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.320
Guessing the key setting which
was used for a given message

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.760
was about as likely as guessing
the outcome of 26 dice roles.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.700
This gave the Germans
confidence that the Allies,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.040
even if they had a
copy of the Enigma,

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.710
could never check all
possible key settings.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.650
For two parties to
communicate using the Enigma,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:49.180
it required that they first
share the daily key settings.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:53.550
This allowed them to align their
machines to the same position.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.640
This protocol changed over
and over during the war

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.270
but generally involved
distributing key sheets

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.330
in advance to all operators.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:06.060
Each day, the operator would
cut off the daily settings.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.260
And this would tell them
the daily configuration

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.500
of their machines, such
as what rotors to use

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.490
and the order of the rotors.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.785
This key setting was then
to be destroyed after use.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.620
However, one vital step
was left to the operator.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.880
They were to select a random
initial position of each rotor

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.030
before communication began.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.370
And a very simple
mistake was made

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.490
by some fatigued operators.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.430
We make this exact
same mistake every time

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.250
we set up a bike
lock combination

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.950
because we tend to
rotate this cylinder only

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.000
a few clicks from
the initial state.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.200
Or we reuse a common password.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.340
This destroyed the
uniform distribution

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.180
of the initial rotor position.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.260
And after repeated observations,
it allowed the Allies

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:59.380
to reverse engineer the
rotor wirings completely.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.750
The second major error
was a design error

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.910
not a procedural one.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:08.150
The Enigma was designed, so
that an input letter would never

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.090
encrypt to itself.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.310
So given an encrypted
letter, such as L,

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.720
you can now eliminate
the possibility

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.780
that L was the original letter.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:22.080
What they thought was
a strength was actually

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.182
a weakness in design.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.890
And this led to a code-breaking
machine initially designed

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:33.820
by the Poles and later improved
by the British American effort.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.559
The bombe was a multiple
Enigma rotors chained together,

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:41.530
allowing it to rapidly test
different key settings.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.360
It took advantage of the
fact that common words

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.840
were known to be in the original
message, such as the weather.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.470
And these came to
be known as cribs.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.880
For a given message
in crib, the bombe

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.490
could scan through all possible
rotor positions and orders

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:59.680
in order to find
possible key settings

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.690
in a matter of minutes.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:04.500
This machine allowed the
Allies to read German commands

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.740
within hours of
them being issued.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.250
It was a fatal blow to
their combat strategy

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:12.570
as the Allies could
anticipate their next move.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.890
One fact remains,
this initial attempt

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:19.540
at automating the
one-time pad failed.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:22.050
If the operators had
instead rolled dice

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:24.480
to decide their initial
rotor positions,

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.120
the starting point
in the sequence

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.110
could have been
uniformly distributed.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.630
This would have prevented
the reverse engineering

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.185
of the rotor wirings.

00:09:33.185 --> 00:09:35.040
And if the Enigma
allowed letters

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.010
to be encrypted to
themselves, the bombe

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.750
could not have taken
advantage of cribs.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.630
And this would have
required the Allies

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:46.040
to check the entire key
space which was impossible,

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.490
even with the fastest computer.

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:52.090
Repetition reduced
the key space.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.370
Otherwise, the outcome
of World War II

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.090
could have been
drastically different.

